        "decision": "approved",
        "decision_rationale": "The retained official Census documentation states that standard 2020 ACS 1-year estimates were not released because pandemic-related collection disruption and nonresponse bias prevented the standard estimates from meeting statistical quality standards. I approve treating standard ACS1 2020 as a whole-vintage nonpublication gap, supported by the exact documentary capture and subject commitments below. The experimental 2020 ACS1 estimates are a different product and must not substitute for the standard release; the separately published ACS5 product is unaffected. This classification is not inferred from a missing acquisition, an HTTP response, or individual-geography absence. It does not authorize fabricated observations, imputation, physical-state acceptance, or activation.",
